.\" DoomWM - dynamic window manager
.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
.TH DOOMWM 1 "August 2025" "doomwm\-VERSION"
.SH NAME
doomwm \- a very dynamic window manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B doomwm
.RB [ \-v ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBDoomWM\fP is a lightweight, tiling window manager for X11 with extra
layouts, adjustable gaps and a
bottom-aligned status bar.  Windows are organised by \fItags\fP, and a view can
display one or many tags at once.  Focus is indicated with a colour-encoded
zero-pixel border.
.P
Key features:
.IP \[bu] 2
Runtime-adjustable 20 px gaps between clients.
.IP \[bu]
Per-tag memory for layout, gaps, master count, bar visibility and master-area
size.
.IP \[bu]
Status bar at the screen bottom (toggleable, fixed height optional).
.IP \[bu]
Plain numbered tag labels, and the bar can host XEmbed system-tray icons.
.IP \[bu]
Additional layouts: \fIspiral\fP, \fIdwindle\fP, \fIcenteredmaster\fP and
\fIcenteredfloatingmaster\fP, alongside \fItile\fP, \fIfloating\fP and
\fImonocle\fP.
.IP \[bu]
Scratch-pad terminal (Mod1-Shift-p) and automatic swallowing of transient
floating windows.
.IP \[bu]
Extensive key bindings for common CLI/TUI and GUI programs; see
.BR KEYBOARD COMMANDS .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-v
Print version information to \fBstderr\fP and exit.
.SH USAGE
.SS Status-bar interaction
.TP
.B Button1
View the clicked tag; clicking the layout symbol toggles between the two most
recent layouts.
.TP
.B Button3
Toggle the clicked tag’s visibility.
.TP
.B Mod1\-Button1
Apply the clicked tag to the focused window.
.TP
.B Mod1\-Button3
Toggle the clicked tag on the focused window.
.SS Keyboard commands
The modifier is \fBMod1\fP (Alt).  Core window-manager bindings:
.TP
.BR Mod1\-Shift\-Return
Launch \fBdoomterm\fP.
.TP
.BR Mod1\-d
Launch \fBdoommenu\fP.
.TP
.BR Mod1\-b
Toggle the status bar.
.TP
.BR Mod1\-t ", " Mod1\-Shift\-y ", " Mod1\-y
Tile, floating or monocle layout.
.TP
.BR Mod1\-i " / " Mod1\-Shift\-i
Centered master / centered floating-master.
.TP
.BR Mod1\-u " / " Mod1\-Shift\-u
Spiral / dwindle.
.TP
.BR Mod1\-space
Restore previous layout.
.TP
.BR Mod1\-j ", " Mod1\-k
Focus next / previous window.
.TP
.BR Mod1\-o ", " Mod1\-p
Increase / decrease master-area client count.
.TP
.BR Mod1\-h ", " Mod1\-l
Shrink / grow master-area width.
.TP
.BR Mod1\-Return
Promote focused window to master.
.TP
.BR Mod1\-Shift\-c
Close focused window.
.TP
.BR Mod1\-Shift\-space
Toggle floating state.
.TP
.BR Mod1\-Tab
Restore previous tag set.
.TP
.BR Mod1\-[1..9] " / " Mod1\-Shift\-[1..9]
View / tag windows.
.TP
.BR Mod1\-0 " / " Mod1\-Shift\-0
View / tag all tags.
.TP
.BR Mod1\--
Decrease gaps.
.TP
.BR Mod1\-=
Increase gaps.
.TP
.BR Mod1\-Shift\-=
Reset gaps to 0.
.TP
.BR Mod1\-Shift\-x
Quit (\fBMod1\-Control\-Shift\-q\fP to restart).
.TP
.BR Mod1\-F11
Start \fBdoomlock\fP, then suspend with \fBloginctl\fP.
.P
See
.BR config.h
for the full, application-specific binding list.
.SS Mouse commands
.TP
.BR Mod1\-Button1
Move window (forces floating).
.TP
.BR Mod1\-Button2
Toggle floating.
.TP
.BR Mod1\-Button3
Resize window (forces floating).
.SH FILES
Startup scripts are loaded from \fB$XDG_DATA_HOME/doomwm\fP. If
\fB$XDG_DATA_HOME\fP is unset, DoomWM uses
\fB$HOME/.local/share/doomwm\fP.
.P
If present, the following scripts are executed:
.TP 15
.B autostart_blocking.sh
Runs synchronously; DoomWM waits for completion.
.TP
.B autostart.sh
Runs asynchronously before the event loop.
.SH CUSTOMISATION
All behaviour is configured in
.BR config.h
and compiled in:
.P
.RS
.B make clean install
.RE
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGHUP
Restart DoomWM (after recompiling).
.TP
.B SIGTERM
Exit cleanly.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR doommenu (1),
.BR doomterm (1)
